{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T16:23:18Z","timestamp":1791390198449,"version":"4.3.3"},"reference-count":20,"publisher":"Institute for Operations Research and the Management Sciences (INFORMS)","issue":"2","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Operations Research"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2016,4]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> In this paper we consider the notion of rectangularity of a set of probability measures from a somewhat different point of view. We define rectangularity as a property of dynamic decomposition of a distributionally robust stochastic optimization problem and show how it relates to the modern theory of coherent risk measures. Consequently, we discuss robust formulations of multistage stochastic optimization problems in frameworks of stochastic programming, stochastic optimal control, and Markov decision processes. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1287\/opre.2015.1466","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,2,15]],"date-time":"2016-02-15T13:58:00Z","timestamp":1455544680000},"page":"528-541","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":34,"title":["Rectangular Sets of Probability Measures"],"prefix":"10.1287","volume":"64","author":[{"given":"Alexander","family":"Shapiro","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Industrial and Systems Engineering, Georgia Institute of Technology, Atlanta, Georgia 30332"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"109","reference":[{"key":"B1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/1467-9965.00068"},{"key":"B2","volume-title":"Stochastic Optimal Control, The Discrete Time Case","author":"Bertsekas DP","year":"1978"},{"key":"B3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4612-1394-9"},{"key":"B4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0022-0531(03)00097-8"},{"key":"B5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","